# Phase 1e-2 (path-tracking refactor): the .cs files in Runtime/ are
# ``buf generate`` artefacts, not hand-written code. They land here
# via the rsync step in Runtime/README.md, but they live canonically
# in cap-spec/gen/csharp/ on the cap repo side and should NOT be
# committed to OperaSim-PhysX (that would create a sync drift risk
# the moment cap-spec/proto changes).
#
# What stays in git: package.json + Runtime/README.md + this
# .gitignore. The rsync step is the contract; Unity treats the
# package as embedded local but the .cs payload is regenerated.
Runtime/*.cs
Runtime/*.cs.meta
